ones{/number}","notifications_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/PrefectHQ/prefect/notifications{?since,all,participating}","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/PrefectHQ/prefect/labels{/name}","releases_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/PrefectHQ/prefect/releases{/id}","deployments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/PrefectHQ/prefect/deployments","created_at":"2018-06-29T21:59:26Z","updated_at":"2025-12-12T19:22:36Z","pushed_at":"2025-12-12T19:28:51Z","git_url":"git://github.com/PrefectHQ/prefect.git","ssh_url":"git@github.com:PrefectHQ/prefect.git","clone_url":"https://github.com/PrefectHQ/prefect.git","svn_url":"https://github.com/PrefectHQ/prefect","homepage":"https://prefect.io","size":195516,"stargazers_count":21075,"watchers_count":21075,"language":"Python","has_issues":true,"has_projects":false,"has_downloads":true,"has_wiki":false,"has_pages":false,"has_discussions":true,"forks_count":2034,"mirror_url":null,"archived":false,"disabled":false,"open_issues_count":1091,"license":{"key":"apache-2.0","name":"Apache License 2.0","spdx_id":"Apache-2.0","url":"https://api.github.com/licenses/apache-2.0","node_id":"MDc6TGljZW5zZTI="},"allow_forking":true,"is_template":false,"web_commit_signoff_required":false,"topics":["automation","data","data-engineering","data-ops","data-science","infrastructure","ml-ops","observability","orchestration","pipeline","prefect","python","workflow","workflow-engine"],"visibility":"public","forks":2034,"open_issues":1091,"watchers":21075,"default_branch":"main","permissions":{"admin":false,"maintain":false,"push":false,"triage":false,"pull":true}},"body":"## Opened from the [Prefect Public Slack Community](https://prefect.io/slack)\n\n**josedanielpm**: Hi! has anyone faced this error when starting Orion? the .db file does not exist, it is new.\n\n**anna**: if you use the latest Orion version, you shouldn't have to bind the host to 0.0.0.0\n\n**anna**: Do you run it from within a Docker container? `prefect orion start` should be sufficient when starting Orion locally\n\n**josedanielpm**: Yes, using the last one and already tried without host option.\n\n**josedanielpm**: And yes, running within a Docker container.\n\n**anna**: Can you try it locally without Docker? This may be much easier\n\n**anna**: check this install guide for troubleshooting <https://orion-docs.prefect.io/getting-started/installation/>\n\n**josedanielpm**: Locally works, what I don't understand is why it doesn't work in the container if it used to work without any problem.\n\nI just wanted to check if anyone knew about the error and had clues on what may cause it.\n\n**anna**: I'd assume it's because the Docker network works differently than your local network, and Orion has services that need to communicate together, and possibly cannot within a Docker network\n\n**anna**: <@ULVA73B9P> open \"Orion: when running 2.0 within Docker container or Google Cloud Shell users get AttributeError: type object 'ORMInsert' has no attribute 'orm_pre_session_exec'\"\n\nOriginal thread can be found [here](https://prefect-community.slack.com/archives/CL09KU1K7/p1648748632449419?thread_ts=1648748632.449419&cid=CL09KU1K7).\n\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/PrefectHQ/prefect/issues/5627/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/PrefectHQ/prefect/issues/5627/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed"}},"event":"cross-referenced"}]